          dealing: 'Five cards each face down; first betting round requires Jacks or Better to open. If someone opens, draw and second betting round as in Five Card Draw. If no one opens, same hand becomes ace-to-five lowball with a new betting round, then draw for low, then final betting and showdown.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the pot by having the best high hand at showdown if someone opened the first betting round, or the best low hand (ace-to-five, straights and flushes do not count) if no one opened and the hand was played as lowball.',
          gameplay: "Ante and deal five cards face down to each player. First betting round: Jacks or Better required to open; if no one opens, the hand is not thrown in—players keep their cards and the game switches to ace-to-five lowball with a new betting round begun by the player to dealer's left. If someone opened, play continues as normal Five Card Draw: each active player may discard and draw up to three replacements, then second betting round, then showdown; highest five-card hand wins. If the hand became lowball, after the new betting round players draw to improve for low, then a final betting round; showdown with lowest hand winning (A-2-3-4-5 is best). Often played with a joker as bug for high and fitter for low.",
          keyRules: [
            'Jacks or Better to open first betting round',
